A||N||2||fieroo||1984 Tech 4   2.5 won't run||||1||
Z||000000||fieroo||12-18-2001||10:58 AM||||I had my 84 tech 4 running great.  Idle like a new car.  Then the tachometer jumped up and down and it shut down.  It restarted just fine.  Two days later,  the tach went crazy and it shut down and has not run since.  It starts and runs for about 30 seconds.  Chugs hard and shuts off.  Any ideas on what this might be?  Plugs were a little dirty but not bad? Wires seem okay.<BR>Any help would be appreciated? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rodrv6||12-18-2001||03:40 PM||||It might be a bad tach filter.  Look for a little round "can" near the ignition coil.  Unplug it and see if the problem is gone.  It is the tach filter and sometimes they go bad.  New ones are no longer available, but Rodney Dickman makes replacements for them.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  <BR>White 88 GT :)||||reg||1
Z||000002||GTDude||12-18-2001||11:00 PM||||I go with the tach filter too......or possible a bad tach.  But I'd try the filter first......you prob need a new one anyway.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/DSCF0003a_1.JPG">  ||||reg||10
